"""
engine_core.py  --  ONE source of truth for realistic XAUUSD trade simulation.

This module is a faithful extraction of the simulation that previously lived
inside ``backtest/realistic_xauusd.py``.  The standalone engine's behaviour is
the authoritative specification; nothing here invents a new strategy or changes
a formula.  ``realistic_xauusd.py`` and ``optimizer_realistic_numba.py`` both
call into this module so the two can never drift apart again.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WAS PORTED (verbatim, from realistic_xauusd.py):
    * ema()                        SMA-seeded EMA, seed at index (period-1)
    * rsi()                        SMA-seeded Wilder RSI, out pre-filled 50.0
    * atr()                        SMA-seeded Wilder ATR.  Seed = mean(TR[1:period+1])
                                   placed at index ``period``.  TR[0] is NOT used.
    * _backtest()                  the whole event loop, bar for bar
    * load_ohlc()  / _load()       CSV load + column normalise + time sort/dedupe
    * prepare_spread()             per-bar spread: points -> price, floored at
                                   DEFAULT_SPREAD, NaN/inf/<=floor -> DEFAULT_SPREAD
    * compute_indicators()         one causal pass over the full series + warmup

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POINT M  --  SAME-BAR RE-ENTRY / STOP-TIMING  (authoritative, from the loop):

  Inspected in realistic_xauusd.py `_backtest`:

  1. NO SAME-BAR RE-ENTRY.
     On bar ``i`` an open position is managed FIRST.  If it closes on bar ``i``
     the guard ``if position != 0 or closed_this_bar: continue`` prevents a new
     entry on that same bar.  The earliest a new position can open after an exit
     on bar ``i`` is bar ``i+1`` (signal read from bar ``i``, filled at
     ``open[i+1]``).

  2. ENTRY BAR IS NOT CHECKED FOR STOP/TARGET.
     A position is opened at the END of the bar-``i`` iteration (filled at
     ``open[i]``).  The stop/target check runs at the TOP of an iteration, so the
     first bar on which this position can be stopped or take profit is bar
     ``i+1``.  Bar ``i``'s own high/low never trigger the stop of a position
     entered on bar ``i``.

  3. Signal uses ONLY completed bar ``i-1`` (ef/es/et/rv/av at ``i-1``); the
     fill is at ``open[i]``.  No bar-``i`` OHLC touches the decision or the fill.

  These three behaviours are preserved exactly and MUST NOT be changed without
  changing realistic_xauusd.py's authoritative loop in lock step.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE ON CONSTANTS:
  The cost / risk / contract constants below are baked into the numba-compiled
  ``run_window_fast`` at compile time.  Mutating ``engine_core.SLIPPAGE`` (etc.)
  from another module after import will NOT affect the compiled kernel.  Change
  the value here, in the single source.
"""

